WEBVTT

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:01.590
CLIFF SIMPKINS: Welcome
to the session.

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:02.370
I'm Cliff Simpkins.

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:04.800
I lead Developer
Relations here at UiPath.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.590
If UiPath isn't on your
radar yet, that's fine.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.640
In the next 20 minutes,

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.980
I'm going to give you a
quick version of what we do,

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.620
why it's relevant to what you're
building, and then I'm going

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.810
to hand you over to
the highlight reel

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:17.880
from our developer conference
that we had three weeks ago

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.420
where you could see real
demos and real code.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.930
UiPath is Microsoft's
preferred enterprise agentic

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.460
automation platform.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.710
It's built on Azure, and
it's deployed to some

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.800
of the most governed enterprise
environments out there.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.410
For developers, there's three
things that are worth knowing.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:38.070
First, UiPath Maestro
provides the execution layer

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.110
that makes your agent
production ready.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.990
It provides governance, it
provides observability,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:46.440
human approvals, and durable
state all out of the box.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.520
It's the enterprise runtime

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.950
that your agents can
deploy right into.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:53.760
Second, if you're using GitHub
Copilot today, you can build

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.890
on UiPath right out of the box.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.040
Install UiPath skills
and CLI using the NPM,

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.620
and Copilot gets full context
on the UiPath platform.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.060
Our APIs are CLI commands

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:06.030
and battle-tested deployment
patterns, and you can even ship

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.100
without leaving
Visual Studio Code.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.250
Third, because UiPath runs on
Azure, you inherit the security,

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.900
identity, and
compliance controls

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.060
that your enterprise
already trusts.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.610
There's nothing new
for you to approve.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.220
Now, most people know
us from our RPA roots,

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.770
but today's platform is
going to be so much more.

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.750
It's now a runtime for
orchestrating complex

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.700
and agentic processes.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.760
It's one of the only platforms
that can manage agents, robots,

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.140
human review steps, system
integrations, and exceptions all

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.190
in a governed auditable
execution environment.

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:40.860
You get to build agentic
automation the way you want.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.750
Our governed execution
layer provides you

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.570
with the flexibility and the
extensibility that you need.

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.000
You can use low-code
tools, pre-built agents,

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.430
and you can even run custom
agents using the tools,

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:53.610
frameworks, and models that
you already use and trust.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.370
You always have secure and
seamless access to your data

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:58.830
without needing to move
it or duplicate it.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:01.260
We provide the data
governance and controls

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:04.860
that meet the most stringent
compliance requirements.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.960
At the core of our
platform is Maestro,

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.150
the UiPath orchestration engine.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:12.480
It handles control flow for your
AI agents, human approval steps,

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.130
and system integrations.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:17.370
It manages state across
long-running processes.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.310
It handles your retries,
timeouts, and partial failures,

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.710
and every process it
runs is observable

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.380
and auditable right
out of the box.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:29.160
Maestro supports three canvases
to model how you operate,

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.320
and you're going to see
all three in action soon.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.560
First, Maestro VPN is our
business process canvas.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.530
Second, Maestro Flow is
our developer canvas.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.870
Third, Maestro Case is
there for your more complex

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:43.320
and dynamic business processes.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.880
Here's what it all
looks like in practice

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.800
for a Microsoft-first
environment.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.830
Most enterprise work
starts in Microsoft 365,

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:54.120
but complex processes such as
claims, loans, approvals tend

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.890
to need a dedicated
orchestration layer

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:59.400
that Copilot just wasn't
designed to be out of the box.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.010
That's where our joint
architecture comes in.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.560
Employees collaborate in
Teams, Outlook, SharePoint,

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.860
and Copilot to orchestrate
open-ended and complex tasks.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.920
Those complex tasks run
in an orchestration layer

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.780
that provides access
to problem-solving,

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.630
dynamic decisions, and
long-running execution

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.300
across documents, desktops,
legacy applications,

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.030
enterprise systems, all
the stuff you need.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:23.220
If a human is needed,
the process can surface

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.620
that back to a human via Teams.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:29.670
Taken together, your Teams, your
users, and your data all live

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:32.310
where they are, and with
an orchestration engine

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.280
that brings them together.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.440
There's two new
Microsoft-focused integrations I

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.550
want to call out.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.610
First, UiPath conversational
agents now run

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.590
in Microsoft Teams.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.240
UiPath agents are
built and deployed

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.210
in UiPath using our extensive
integration service connectors,

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:51.420
and once built, you can deploy
the agent using a standard Teams

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.580
packaging process,
and at that point,

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:57.090
your employees can use your
agents in one-on-one chats

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.040
or in channel-based workflows.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.350
Employees submit information,
check process status,

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:04.860
and receive updates all
without leaving Teams.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.200
Second, Copilot can now
unlock the capabilities

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.940
of the UiPath platform.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:12.180
You install the UiPath
skills and CLI using NPM,

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:15.240
and Copilot gets full context
about our platform, APIs,

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:17.600
CLI commands,
deployment patterns.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.400
From that point forward,
you can build, deploy,

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.620
and manage your
agentic automations

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:25.590
on UiPath using the coding
agent that you love.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:27.450
Let me hand you off
to our product team.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.920
Three weeks ago in Bengaluru,

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.080
UiPath ran our day-long
developer conference,

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:34.490
and I've cut our keynote
down to about 15 minutes.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:37.010
We're going to explore
four UiPath innovations.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.210
First, our engineers are going

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.340
to use their favorite coding
agents to build, debug,

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:43.010
and deploy their
automations on UiPath.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:45.800
Second, Maestro Flow is
going to be shown off,

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.830
which is our new visual canvas
with full Visual Studio code

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.640
and coding agent support.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.170
Third, we're going to
show off Maestro Case

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:54.900
for orchestrating complex
exception-driven processes,

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:58.200
and last, our new agentic
testing capabilities.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.910
RAGHU MALPANI: The
world of development,

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:00.840
automation development

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.320
and software development
has dramatically changed

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.510
in the last 12 months,
more so than it changed

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.880
in the last two decades.

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:11.270
Forty percent or more of
code is now generated by AI.

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:12.020
Eighty-five percent

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.690
of developers use coding
agents to do their work now.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:19.500
Everything we're announcing
today is centered on this idea

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.020
about making you, the
developer, the builder,

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:25.530
the most leveraged
person in your company.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:27.720
This is what
leverage looks like.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.220
Same five stages,

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.220
but dramatically
different timelines.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.590
The building and planning
phases compress in time

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:37.680
from months to hours and days.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:42.420
Debugging, deploying,
testing compresses to hours.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:44.010
When you have an
incident in production,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:47.100
a coding agent can begin work
