the issue in minutes.

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:50.910
ALEXANDRU ROMAN: I
have created a process

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:57.030
that automates onboarding new
hires in an online portal.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:57.990
It's Friday.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:01.080
Everything worked
perfectly until it didn't.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:05.940
I'm using Claude Code,
and I am asking its help

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:09.480
to investigate why
this queue is failing.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:12.720
It's doing everything you would
do as a human, but faster.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.250
It goes to Orchestrator.

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:15.780
It reads the logs.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:20.070
It investigates the target
systems, and creating hypotheses

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:25.260
and testing them to make sure it
really identifies why it failed.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:29.580
In my case, the target
system blocked APIs.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:34.020
It did a big analysis, and
it gave me a clear timeline,

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:37.620
when this happened, why it
happened, and it suggests

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.840
to me how to solve for this.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:44.430
Basically, I said, okay
Claude, now go and fix it,

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:45.870
and what is happening right now?

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:48.570
It's basically going
through the existing code,

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:50.970
going through the
recommendation,

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:53.280
and starts working with it.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:57.360
Since it's an API automation,
now switch to a new eye.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:59.850
It's looking at my target
system, and it tries

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.760
to identify the needed element.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:04.410
I fast-forwarded half an hour,

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:08.040
and you can see what the
coding agent built for me.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:12.030
It created object repository,
UI files, and so on.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:16.380
We can see all the needed
actions like filling the form,

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:21.030
typing in the right
inputs, so in minutes,

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:24.960
I was able to investigate
and come up with a fix.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:28.500
It's building the package and
it's pushing it to Orchestrator.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.290
We provide a set
of tools and CLIs

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:36.450
that give your agents full
control to the platform,

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.850
and everything is
in the same trusted

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:42.150
and governed environment.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:44.250
This time, I'm using Gemini CLI.

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:47.190
Remember that our coding
agent support is agnostic

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:50.940
of the platform, so you
can use whatever you like.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:56.370
In this case, the coding
agent goes through the PDD.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:57.990
It understands what
it needs to do.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:00.540
It recommends me how
to structure my code.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.610
In this case, I
should do a producer

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:05.220
and a consumer and use a queue.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:09.870
You get coding agents to help
you from build to troubleshoot

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:12.330
to production and back.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:14.280
VIKRAM KAKUMANI: Last year,
